<!--
  The Radio Myata mark on its own, for the system splash.

  Same geometry as ic_launcher_foreground, with two of its eight paths removed and
  nothing added:

    dropped   the radial-gradient rounded square - the yellow launcher plate;
    dropped   the 15% white sheen, which is drawn on that plate's shape and is
              meaningless without it;
    kept      the green fill, its outline and the four shading paths, unchanged.

  So this is not a redesign. It is the existing mark with its plate taken off,
  which is what the launcher plate was: a container for the icon grid, not part of
  the mark.

  Sizing. The framework maps this 108 viewport onto the splash icon box, which
  measured ~290dp on both API levels, so apparent size is set by how much of the
  viewport the art occupies - exactly the adaptive-icon contract, and the reason
  the plate rendered at 184dp: it filled 63.5% of the viewport.

  The group below is ic_launcher_foreground's own transform with the scale reduced
  and the translation recomputed to keep the mark centred:

    scale       0.5030783 -> 0.3128
    translate   19.68 -> 32.05, 32.25

  The mark's own bounds are ~107.1 x 89.8 in the group's units, so 0.3128 puts it
  at ~33.5 x 28.1 of 108, or 31% x 26% of the viewport - about 90 x 75dp rendered.
  Verified on device rather than assumed; the measured result is in
  tools/qa/splash/launch-sequence.json.
-->
